itical party in canada. Conservative Party of Canada is a political party in Ottawa, established in 2003-12-07. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The Conservative Party of Canada (CPC), formed on December 7, 2003, in Ottawa, represents a critical evolution in Canadian political history. Its establishment followed the merger of the Canadian Alliance and the Progressive Conservative Party, marking a significant consolidation of right-leaning political forces in Canada. The party has become a major player in Canadian federal politics, influencing the direction of policies on economic management, social issues, and Canada’s role on the global stage. Key figures in its history include Stephen Harper, who served as Prime Minister from 2006 to 2015, and Erin O'Toole, who led the party during the 2021 federal election.

